            <h4 style="color: #002147; border-bottom: 2px solid #004080; padding-bottom: 5px; font-size:20px; font-weight:600;">About Dr. Arvind Kumar Verma</h4>
            <p style="font-size:16px; font-family:Arial; line-height:30px; text-align:justify; line-height:30px;color:black;">
                Dr. Arvind Kumar Verma is working as an Assistant Professor in the Department of Applied Science (Physics) at Bharat Ratna Babasaheb Bhimrao Ambedkar Rajkiya Engineering College Pratapgarh. Currently, he is serving as the Registrar & Dean Academics at BRBBA Rajkiya Engineering College Pratapgarh. His research interest includes, Chalcogenides glass. He has obtained his Ph.D. from University of Lucknow in 2018. Before Ph.D., he has worked as Assistant Professor in the Department of Science at Aryavart Institute of Higher education, Lucknow for two years. He has completed his M.Sc. (Physics) and B.Sc. (PCM) from University of Lucknow. Dr. Arvind   has published more than 20 research papers in reputed International/national journals and conferences. He has co-author of two books (Applied Physics-I & II) published by Asian Publishers for diploma students.  He is a member of Laser and Spectroscopy Society of India.
            </p>


